Assignment ('log_parameter_max_length_on_error', '3') extracted from "The ideal value, for most use cases, is to increase the value for max_wal_size such that it can hold at least one hour's worth of logs. The caveat here, however, is that you do not want to set this value extremely high, as it can increase the amount of time needed for crash recovery. If desired, the min_wal_size can also be increased, so that the system can handle spikes in WAL usage during batch jobs and other unusual circumstances. After making the appropriate configuration changes, and reloading Postgres, we can validate that the new settings are applied, as we expect:
name
setting
------------------------------+-----------
